# Season 0 content · English. Keyed by date: (title, text or platform, note, why, alt(title, platform, note, why) or None)
# Only fields that change; book/song/film titles stay in their original language.
EN = {
 '2026-11-27': ('Caffeine boosts your performance', 'The International Society of Sports Nutrition concludes that 3 to 6 mg of caffeine per kilo of body weight, about 60 minutes before, improves strength and endurance performance. If you train late, it can cost you sleep; if you have high blood pressure or are sensitive to it, ask a professional first.', '', 'If you have coffee before training, this is how to use it without losing sleep.'),
 '2026-11-28': ('Eating slowly fills you up more', 'In a study with women, eating the same meal slowly, with small bites and chewing well, led them to eat about 70 kcal less than eating fast, and they felt just as full or fuller.', '', 'A free trick to eat less without going hungry.'),
 '2026-11-29': ('Plant protein builds muscle too', 'Plant protein usually has less leucine, the amino acid that most switches on muscle building. A review concludes that you can make up for it by combining sources (legumes, grains, soy) and eating a bit more of it.', '', 'If you eat little meat, you can still build muscle.'),
 '2026-11-30': ('Low-fat or low-carb: it does not matter', 'In the DIETFITS study, 609 adults followed a healthy low-fat or healthy low-carb diet for a year. They lost similar weight, and neither genetics nor insulin predicted who did better on each one.', '', 'The best diet is the one you can keep.'),
 '2026-12-01': (None, 'YouTube · Spotify · Apple Music', '', 'A steady-rhythm riff to warm up with energy.'),
 '2026-12-02': ('Muscle soreness is not lactic acid', 'Muscle soreness is not caused by lactic acid. Back in 1983, a study compared downhill and level running: downhill running caused much more muscle soreness with less lactate in the blood. The pain that shows up 24 to 72 hours later comes from tiny injuries in the fibres and the inflammation that starts their repair, especially after the lowering phase of a lift.', '', 'If it hurts tomorrow, you will know it is not "acid" and that you can move gently.'),
 '2026-12-03': ('Skipping meals does not slow your metabolism', 'In a study with healthy people who fasted for 84 hours, resting energy expenditure did not drop: it rose about 14 % by the third day, due to higher noradrenaline. The "starvation mode" that slows metabolism comes with weeks of eating too little, not with a short fast.', '', 'So you can fast without fearing you will "break" your metabolism.'),
 '2026-12-04': (None, 'YouTube · Spotify · Apple Music', '', 'For the day you come back after a few days off: coming back is what counts.'),
 '2026-12-05': (None, 'Bookshops · eBook · Audiobook', 'True crime, tough content', 'For your rest day: a gripping read that helps you switch off.', ('Atomic Habits – James Clear (2018)', 'Bookshops · eBook · Audiobook', '', 'Small changes that add up every day: the same idea as your streak.')),
 '2026-12-06': ('Protein burns calories while you digest it', 'Digesting protein uses 20 to 30 % of its calories, compared with 5 to 10 % for carbohydrates and 0 to 3 % for fats. It is also the most filling nutrient, which is why protein-rich meals keep you satisfied for longer.', '', 'It helps you choose meals that fill you up and look after your muscle.'),
 '2026-12-07': ('How much water you need a day', 'The European Food Safety Authority sets an adequate total water intake of 2.0 litres a day for women and 2.5 litres for men, counting the water in food (about 20 %). From drinks, that is about 1.6 and 2.0 litres. Heat and exercise raise your needs. A practical guide: pale yellow urine means you are well hydrated; dark urine means you need more water.', '', 'So you know how much to drink for your body, without memorised numbers.'),
 '2026-12-08': ('Fat leaves through your lungs', 'When you lose 10 kg of fat, about 8.4 kg leave as carbon dioxide when you breathe and the rest as water. Breathing faster will not slim you down: what matters is using more energy than you eat.', '', 'Knowing where fat goes clears up a lot of myths.'),
 '2026-12-09': ('The Wild Project – episodes with Javier Santaolalla', 'YouTube · Spotify · Apple Podcasts', 'Episodes #311 and #348 are only on YouTube. In Spanish', 'Science told with passion: understanding how the world works trains your mind too. Great for listening while you walk.'),
 '2026-12-10': ('The anabolic window is wide', 'A meta-analysis found that the supposed benefit of having protein right after training disappeared once total daily protein was matched. What matters most is how much protein you eat over the day, spread over several meals.', '', 'So you do not have to rush to eat after training if you are not hungry.'),
 '2026-12-11': (None, 'PC · Xbox Series X|S · PS5', 'Action to the beat of the music', 'Everything moves to the beat of the music, like a good workout. A treat for your day off.'),
 '2026-12-12': ('Your first strength comes from your brain', 'In the first weeks of training, almost all the strength you gain comes from your nervous system, not new muscle. A classic study measured the electrical activity of muscles and saw that fibre recruitment improves first, and muscle growth takes over later. That is why beginners add weight fast without looking bigger.', '', 'It explains why you add weight quickly at first even though muscle takes longer.'),
 '2026-12-13': (None, 'Rent or buy depending on your country (check JustWatch)', 'Won 3 Oscars', 'About extreme discipline and its price: push yourself, yes; break yourself, no.'),
 '2026-12-14': ('Hunger keeps a schedule', 'Ghrelin, the hunger hormone, rises just before your usual meal times and drops after you eat. That is why, when you start fasting, hunger shows up at fixed times. With consistency, your body gets used to the new schedule.', '', 'It helps you choose your eating window so you feel less hungry.'),
 '2026-12-15': ('Liquid calories do not fill you up', 'In a study, adding 450 kcal a day as soft drinks made people gain weight, because they did not eat less afterwards. When the same calories came from solid jelly sweets, they made up for it by eating less the rest of the day.', '', 'An easy change: what you drink counts too.'),
 '2026-12-16': (None, 'Bookshops · eBook', 'It has a Netflix series. In Spanish', 'A story about chasing what you truly want, to switch off on your rest day.'),
 '2026-12-17': ('Moving without noticing', '16 people ate 1,000 extra kcal a day for 8 weeks. Some gained up to 10 times more fat than others, and the difference was explained by movement outside exercise: standing, walking, fidgeting.', '', 'Steps and moving through the day add up more than you think.'),
 '2026-12-18': ('Neverender – Justice and Tame Impala', 'YouTube · Spotify · Apple Music', '', 'Electronic music with a steady pulse, perfect for easy cardio or stretching.'),
 '2026-12-19': ('Light weights build muscle too', 'A meta-analysis found that training with light loads (down to 30 % of your max) close to failure produces muscle growth similar to heavy loads. Maximal strength, however, improves more with heavy weights.', '', 'If you train at home or with little weight, you still make progress.'),
 '2026-12-20': ('You do not need to reach failure', 'A meta-analysis comparing training to failure with stopping short found no significant difference in muscle growth. Stopping 1 to 3 reps short of failure causes less fatigue and helps you recover for the next session, as long as the sets are hard.', '', 'Training close to failure is enough: less risk, same gains.'),
 '2026-12-21': ('Fasted cardio: same fat loss', 'A 4-week study of young women in a calorie deficit compared fasted cardio with cardio after eating. Both groups lost the same weight and fat. What decides it is your daily balance, not the time of the session.', '', 'So you can train whenever suits you, not because of myths.'),
 '2026-12-22': (None, 'Netflix', 'Won the Oscar for best documentary; about doping', 'What happens when people chase performance at any cost. In PandarIA, no shortcuts.'),
 '2026-12-23': ('The fibre almost nobody eats', 'A large analysis commissioned by the WHO found that people who eat 25 to 29 g of fibre a day have 15 to 30 % lower mortality and less heart disease, type 2 diabetes and colorectal cancer than people who eat little.', '', 'A simple way to eat better and feel fuller.'),
 '2026-12-24': (None, 'YouTube · Spotify · Amazon Music', 'Not on Apple Podcasts. In Spanish', 'Short reflections on life and consistency, to listen to while you walk.'),
 '2026-12-25': ('Enjoy today without guilt', 'One big meal does not undo weeks of work: what changes your body is what you repeat every day, not what you do on one day. Enjoy dinner with your loved ones, drink water and, if you feel like it, go for a 10-minute walk after eating: it helps lower the blood sugar spike.', '', 'Enjoying yourself is part of a healthy life too. Merry Christmas!'),
 '2026-12-26': ('Overeating does not build more muscle', 'Elite athletes who followed a planned calorie surplus gained more weight than those who ate freely, but much of that extra weight was fat. A moderate surplus is enough to build muscle.', '', 'So you build muscle without gaining extra fat.'),
 '2026-12-27': ('How to hydrate when you train', 'The 2015 international consensus on exercise-associated hyponatraemia recommends drinking to thirst, not beyond it: forcing yourself to drink too much dilutes the sodium in your blood and has caused deaths in athletes. In long or hot sessions, weigh yourself before and after: each kilo lost is roughly a litre of sweat, and to replace it drink 1.25 to 1.5 litres per kilo, ideally with some salt or food.', '', 'It tells you how much to drink before, during and after training.'),
 '2026-12-28': ('The Man Who Mistook His Wife for a Hat – Oliver Sacks (1985)', 'Bookshops · eBook', 'Real neurological cases told by a neurologist', 'How the brain builds who you are. Your first strength comes from there.'),
 '2026-12-29': ('Long stretches before lifting cost strength', 'A large review found that holding a static stretch for more than 60 seconds per muscle right before training slightly reduces immediate strength and power, while short stretches barely matter. To warm up, move and do light sets of the exercise itself.', '', 'So you warm up well without losing strength before you lift.'),
 '2026-12-30': ('Fallout (seasons 1 and 2)', 'Prime Video', 'Adult series', 'Recovering is training too: a series for your day off.', ('Cobra Kai', 'Netflix', 'For ages 14 and up', 'Consistency, discipline and second chances, on the mat.')),
 '2026-12-31': ('16:8 is not magic', 'Two major clinical trials compared eating within a time window with a normal diet of the same calories: one lasting 12 weeks with 116 adults and another lasting a year with 139 people with obesity. In neither did the restricted schedule lead to more weight loss. Its advantage is that it makes eating less easier for some people.', '', 'The best fast is the one you can keep.'),
 '2027-01-01': ('Resolutions that last: start small', 'A study followed 96 people as they built a new habit: on average it took 66 days to become automatic, with a lot of variation between people, and missing one day did not ruin the process. Start with something small you can repeat, choose when and where you will do it, and let PandarIA keep count.', '', 'Your streak and your 66 days start with one small step. Happy New Year!'),
 '2027-01-02': ('Weights at 90', '90-year-olds who did 8 weeks of intense strength training increased their strength by 174 % on average and gained thigh muscle. It is never too late to start.', '', 'It is never too late to start getting stronger.'),
 '2027-01-03': ('I Had Some Help – Post Malone and Morgan Wallen', 'YouTube · Spotify · Apple Music', '', 'For training with company: asking for help is progress too.'),
 '2027-01-04': ('Your metabolism adapts', 'Six years after a TV weight-loss competition, contestants burned about 500 kcal a day less at rest than expected for their size. Your body defends itself when you lose a lot of weight, which is why keeping it off takes consistency.', '', 'So you do not lose heart when your weight stalls.'),
 '2027-01-05': ('Creatine: the most studied supplement', 'The International Society of Sports Nutrition considers creatine the most effective supplement for increasing high-intensity training capacity and lean mass, and safe for healthy people at recommended doses (3 to 5 g a day). If you have kidney disease, ask a professional first.', '', 'If you plan to take something, start with what has the most science behind it.'),
 '2027-01-06': ('Resting 3 minutes builds more muscle', 'In an 8-week study of trained men, those who rested 3 minutes between sets gained more thigh muscle thickness and strength than those who rested 1 minute. Resting enough lets you lift more in the following sets.', '', 'Resting between sets is not wasted time.'),
 '2027-01-07': ('Stories by H. P. Lovecraft', 'Free and legal on Wikisource (public domain) · Bookshops', 'Publishers\' translations have their own rights', 'Short stories to read before bed instead of scrolling: your sleep will thank you.'),
 '2027-01-08': ('Performing during Ramadan', 'A review of athletes who fast from dawn to sunset during Ramadan concluded that performance can be maintained by looking after training times, sleep, hydration and what you eat during the permitted hours.', '', 'If you fast for your faith, you can still train wisely.'),
 '2027-01-09': ('Ultra-processed food: 500 kcal more a day', '20 adults lived for a month in a research centre: two weeks on ultra-processed food and two on minimally processed food, eating as much as they wanted. On ultra-processed food they ate about 500 kcal more a day and gained almost a kilo in two weeks.', '', 'Eating less processed food helps without counting every calorie.'),
 '2027-01-10': ('Water before meals', 'In a 12-week trial with dieting adults aged 55 to 75, those who drank 500 ml of water 30 minutes before each meal lost about 2 kg more than those who only dieted. Note: thirst fades with age, so older adults should drink even when they are not very thirsty.', '', 'A simple habit that may help you eat less.'),
 '2027-01-11': ('Sit-ups do not burn belly fat', 'In a study, 6 weeks of abdominal exercises did not reduce belly fat or waist size more than in the group that did not do them. Fat is lost from your whole body, not from the area you train.', '', 'So you do not waste time on what does not work.'),
 '2027-01-12': ('How much protein to build muscle', 'A meta-analysis of 49 studies with more than 1,800 people found that the benefit of protein for building muscle levels off at 1.6 g per kilo of body weight a day, although some people may use up to about 2.2 g.', '', 'So you know how much protein is right for you.'),
 '2027-01-13': (None, 'PC · PS4 · PS5 · Xbox One · Xbox Series X|S', 'PEGI 18', 'Planning, adapting and being patient, like a good training programme. For your day off.', ('Ring Fit Adventure (2019)', 'Nintendo Switch', '', 'A video game that really gets you moving.')),
 '2027-01-14': (None, 'YouTube · Spotify · Apple Music', '', 'Starting again with energy, like your training after the holidays.'),
 '2027-01-15': ('Muscle grows for up to 48 hours', 'Training is only the signal. Measuring muscle protein synthesis showed it stays raised for up to 48 hours after a weights session in untrained people. Muscle is built while you rest and eat, not while you lift.', '', 'That is why your plan leaves days between sessions for the same muscle.'),
 '2027-01-16': ('Eating dinner early counts too', 'In a trial with men with prediabetes, eating everything within 6 hours and finishing before 3 pm improved insulin sensitivity and blood pressure in 5 weeks, without weight loss. It is a small study, but it suggests timing matters too.', '', 'You do not need a long fast: eating dinner earlier also helps.'),
 '2027-01-17': ('How much sugar the WHO recommends', 'The WHO recommends keeping added sugar below 10 % of daily calories, and ideally below 5 %: about 25 grams on a 2,000 kcal diet. A single can of soft drink can go over that.', '', 'So you can cut sugar without banning anything.'),
 '2027-01-18': ('Losing slowly protects muscle', 'Elite athletes who lost 0.7 % of their weight per week gained lean mass and strength, while those who lost 1.4 % per week did not gain lean mass. Losing a bit more slowly preserves muscle better.', '', 'Losing slowly is how you keep what was so hard to build.'),
 '2027-01-19': (None, 'Bookshops · eBook', 'The Big Brother novel', 'A classic that invites you to think for yourself, fitness fads included.'),
 '2027-01-20': ('Muscle memory is real', 'In mice, the nuclei that muscle fibres gain as they grow stay for months even when the muscle shrinks. That would help explain why you regain muscle much faster after a break.', '', 'If you stop for a while, you will get back faster than you think.'),
 '2027-01-21': ('I Play Rocky (2026)', 'Still in cinemas', '', 'How Rocky was born: consistency when nobody believes in you.'),
 '2027-01-22': ('How many daily steps matter', 'A meta-analysis of 15 studies with almost 50,000 people found that the risk of death falls as daily steps rise, levelling off at about 6,000 to 8,000 steps in people over 60 and about 8,000 to 10,000 in people under 60.', '', 'Every step adds up, and you do not need 10,000 to notice it.'),
 '2027-01-23': ('Weight that drops fast is water', 'On very low-calorie diets or fasts of several days, much of the weight lost at first is glycogen and the water stored with it. When you eat again, that weight comes back. Fat is lost more slowly than the scale shows in those first days.', '', 'So the scale in your first week neither scares nor fools you.'),
 '2027-01-24': (None, 'YouTube · Spotify · Apple Music', 'Explicit lyrics', 'Pure energy for the last heavy set of the day.', ('Eye of the Tiger – Survivor', 'YouTube · Spotify · Apple Music', '', 'The classic for the last heavy set of the day.')),
 '2027-01-25': ('Spicy food helps only a little', 'A meta-analysis found that capsaicin from chilli slightly raises energy expenditure and somewhat reduces appetite, but the effect is small, a few dozen calories. It adds flavour without calories, but it does not replace a deficit.', '', 'So you do not expect miracles from any food.'),
 '2027-01-26': (None, 'YouTube · Spotify · Apple Music', 'Explicit lyrics', 'A rhythm that changes suddenly, like HIIT.', ("Don't Stop Me Now – Queen", 'YouTube · Spotify · Apple Music', '', 'Energy to keep going in your HIIT.')),
 '2027-01-27': ('Fitness bands inflate calories', 'Stanford tested 7 bands and watches: most measured heart rate well, but none calculated calories burned accurately. The most accurate was off by 27 % on average and the worst by 93 %.', '', 'So you do not blindly trust your watch\'s calories.'),
 '2027-01-28': ('Training the muscle when stretched', 'In a study, doing triceps extensions with the arm overhead, where the muscle works more stretched, grew the triceps more than doing them with the arm by the side. Training the full range of motion, especially the stretched part, is linked to more muscle. This evidence is recent and still being studied.', '', 'A new way to train backed by recent evidence.'),
 '2027-01-29': ('Short sleep costs muscle', 'Dieters slept 8.5 or 5.5 hours for two weeks. They lost similar weight, but with short sleep they lost 55 % less fat and 60 % more lean mass, and they were hungrier.', '', 'Sleep is part of your plan, not an extra.'),
 '2027-01-30': ('Almonds have fewer calories', 'Measured in people, a 28 g handful of almonds provides about 129 kcal, not the 170 on the label. Some of their fat stays trapped in the cell walls and is not absorbed.', '', 'An example that not every calorie on a label counts the same.'),
 '2027-01-31': ('What people who keep the weight off do', 'The US National Weight Control Registry follows thousands of people who lost a lot of weight and kept it off. Most do about an hour of activity a day, eat breakfast, weigh themselves often and eat in a similar way every day.', '', 'The habits of people who succeeded, so you can take the ones that suit you.'),
}
